        <p>1 Mr. J. Murray, late of the Royal Marine Artillery, heel awn service in India, the Mediterranean and other oess, in well-known 'Mimi el war. It Isaa,tneref ore ,with -Pep regret, that, at the age of thirty-the, r,lie find to give up Her Majeety'a service in which, it opportunity had occurred,he might hate honourably thetinguishid "In 'he year 1392." he said t.. an •• Aberdeen Joinnal " commissioner, who called on hits at Lie house (104,1 hapelatreet, Aberdeen), "I was e 'igen 11,1 opera, linlin in connection with the raitinn of H.M.S. Howe on the Spanish rout, and during the operation. I wee ennetantly wearing wet clothes. At that particular time I did not experience any ill effects. Early In November of the following near, I was on hoard H.M.S. •Einprtm of India 'at Gibraltar. I then began to feel the lower part 01 my back getting very lime, on much so that I could not bend without severe pain. In gehruary, 1894, I got much wore., big continued at work, being unwilling to go sick. In May, 111104, I was paid oft the vessel ill.hl&lt;il I wee eerving,and going Int. barrack., I was three months In tonnage!. fernporarily renewed, I went on hoard H.hl 14. Royal Sovereign,' and, being rattier highly qualified. I got • compsratively easy j .1,, and reas- oned t natty on for Irmo time, although still suffering ptin I continued to net wore., however, and in Octo- ber, 1896, my lege got painfully Swollen, and I experi- enced thematic pains and stiffness at the knee mints. My shoulder joints alei swelled or. and I ma. finally Invalided home from Spain, whore our ship waa lying at the time. I went info hospital, and remained there for shout three months, and receiving no benefit I left the hospital no the 10th March I then commenced taking Dr. William,' Pink Pill, for Pale People, and derived great benefit. as I will prove to you " Mr. \fumy at this point appealed to tie landlady, who completely c.mfirmeel his etatement He added, " Thanks to my cure by Dr. William.