      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1897-06-25_WidnesExaminer_art0012" n="art0012">
        <head>LADIES' LETTER.</head>
        <p>LADIES' LETTER.</p>
        <p>Mr Du,. Nmus,</p>
        <p>Hat• are f the nirienr, and in their rhaphan. nun ..louds of gauze and unto of pantel.like acttnens. 1%. I.a. Llr'ular in quite a manta already, and it. rusty: likely to increase even more.</p>
        <p>One of the lateet noveltiee in hate is of goltlen• ...haired 'draw, with a bond of black ribbon velvet , ai the base of the crown, and thick piliLetlo white tulle juet above it. At the left nide cliviter of choice block oetrich tipe, with a w te ni,ette, and on the left isa bow of niaike.colinn elk, caught with a diamond buckle. A hat ns gr..y straw truntned with eilver.spangleil gory tulle is particularly pretty. At the aide there are loops of very fine white lace cleverly mingled with long.stemnied deep crimson carnatione, and .incler the brim at the aide .t re folds of corded elk of precisely the sante colour an the flowers. The styliith hat, by the way, is intended to be worn with a dress that has a skirt of it aitin•ray aci.vr• 'lion-pleated grey cashmere, and a bodice of grey 4 elk triton.] with eilver.spangled galon, and Leg a pooch vest of white lane over crimson</p>
