      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1897-06-25_WidnesExaminer_art0099" n="art0099">
        <head>EXA</head>
        <p>THE EXA</p>
        <p>tim. ileum Lin OF JUBILIS HONOURS. Mr. David Gamble, CS, of St. Helene, has had the dignity of a baronetcy conferred upon him. The following have been made magistrates for St. Helena :—Jesse Boydell,Cowley flill-lane ; J.Oreen, West Park; James Wilton Nl.Tear, St. Michael's Reim, Rainhill ; Aaron Harper Mitchell. The Dollies, Cowley Hill. FORTUNATE INSBRIATRe. At the Police Station Earlestnwn, on Monday morning, throe men named Lemons. Vinci;, of Clarence-street. Jame Topping, of liajelock, and John Jones, of no fixed address, were charged with being drunk, before Sir Borron. After pleading guilty, the magistrates let them go with a caution. remarking that the leniency was shown to them because of the Jubilee oilier Majesty,</p>
        <p>VIADUCT INSTITUTE BOWLING CLUE. In connection with the above club a bowling handicap wav played on the club green on Satur- day for Mr. lames Lythgoe'e prize. There were :4 entries, and the bowling wee very good until near the Swab, when rain set in and the conditions were rendered unfavourable. rho fleet prim of a capper kettle wan won by James Clough, 2nd be. 1., D. Sherlock, 3rd. 3,,1'. Davies.</p>
        <p>FoRORMRSea. PICNIC FROM EARI.RWrown. On Monday eeveral of the forgemen and smiths employed at the Viaduct workt had a picnic to Worksop and the Dukeriel. The party numbering I 27 left EarlastoWn at :1 o'clock on Monday morning) ! wagonette to Warrington. joined th M.S. and U. Co.'s train at the Central Union, o which a special saloon was provided. On arriteal at Worksop, the headquartere were made at the Greyhound llotel,where a substantial brenkfaat was , pert eken of. After the meal the party drove through the Dukeri,s, visiting Thoresby Howie, the Major (Ink. and Welbeck Abbey, returning to Workmp, whore dinner War heartily enjoyed. Worksop Was lit behind soon aft .tr soven o'clock and Earlemowu was reached at 10.30, the outing having been thoroughly enjoyable. All the arrangetnente,which were carried out by Mr. E. Bennett, gave the ut MOM satisfaction.</p>
        <p>Goon TIOIPLLits. The usual weekly nesnton of the hope of Earle,- town Lodge was held on Monday evening. Bro. T, Cutler presided over a gas( et' Peden., of members and (Orman. On- candidate wan admitted and nevem] proponed. Arrangements were made to re- ceive the Latchford Lodge on Monday next, the I,dge to be opened to he public at 5.30. The Lodge decided that members walk in the St. Helens ri,mopstripion on Tuesday June 22nd, the occasion of the Quesn',. Diamond Jubilee Celebration. The programme for the evening wax." Jubilee Social ' which was well carried out, thanka being tendered to thane who had taken ou active part in providing the refreshmentn. A very enjoyable evening closed in the usual way.</p>
      </div>
