        <head>PA Dli ATE.</head>
        <p>PA Dli ATE.</p>
        <p>DEATH OF MR. WILLIAM ROMON.</p>
        <p>We regret to hart to record the death of Mr. William Noyeton who peasel away at his resioence Paddington flange, at half-past eight on Sunday morning at the age of fin year.. Deceased cote traded a cold • few week. ago which was followed by pneumonia, end. despite the efforta of his medical attendantt caueed hie death an alio., stated Mr. Rovetoo who was • chemical ortnu- lecturer was for many years Coot-chairman on the Highway Dowd. He man Oho a Mataller Of ins Parish Council having occupied the position Cl , Chairman and Vies-chairman and he was Vice- I chairman of that Conned up to the time of hie! death: Ilia lon, will he deeply lamented by • large I circle of friendt especially the members of Christ I Church where he was tor tarter. years {War', warden and for the last few years sideman. Ile was la constant attendee at church and took great In- ternet in religious work. The Rev. J. J. Laughlin., I retorting 10th. eat/event from the pulpit on Sun- day morning said the death of Mr. Royston wee • gnat lone to the &amp;lurch and to the people ; he hed been • long end oarlit•*/ worker amongst them and would be minced by all connected with the ,hurch. The Bag which had been hewed on the church for the Jubilee celebration. 1.11, lowered hall-mast. Deresee4 leaves • widow, four sone sad three daughters with whom this deepest sympathy is felt. The funeral took place at Christ Churchyard on Wedneeday afternoon where • large number of people hail ..mbled. The Rev. J. J. Lengharn was the officiating clergy- man. Amongst those at the graveside were Morris, Frank and Percy Royston, non.; Krne*t Royeton,' nephew Meow, 11. Thornton, T. 11. Orange, 0.1 Mather, J. L. Ilarringten,o Wellier.and membere of the Parish Council ; Mexers. Rafferty., South and Turner,employdee; St . Wm, Bennett, K. Richardeon, John Ilooghton. Thom. Houghton,. Willieto Houghton, J.P., Jam. Mason, J...pb Critchley, F. Wright, Percy Bennett, James Hough- ton, Jar, pti W. Houghton, 0. Bettoli.Alf